		summary = "A **ribosome** is a ribonucleoprotein particle found in all [[Cell (biology)|cells]] that synthesizes [[Protein|proteins]] by [[Translation (biology)|translating]] genetic information encoded in messenger RNA (mRNA). During [[Translation (biology)|translation]], the ribosome decodes successive codons in an mRNA molecule and, with the aid of transfer RNA (tRNA), links [[Amino acid|amino acids]] into a polypeptide chain. Each ribosome comprises a small and a large subunit, each composed of one or more ribosomal RNA (rRNA) molecules and many ribosomal proteins.",
